3. Commercial License Required
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

A separate written commercial license from the Licensor is required for
any of the following uses of the Software:

  (a) Commercial SaaS: offering a hosted or subscription service whose
      user interface is built with the Software, where customers pay to
      access the service;
  (b) Commercial Software Products: distributing or licensing software
      products that include the Software, whether sold perpetually, by
      subscription, or otherwise commercially;
  (c) Paid Customer Delivery: using the Software to build applications,
      portals, or systems that You deliver to a customer or client in
      exchange for payment, including consulting, outsourcing, and
      system-integration engagements, even when the resulting system is
      used only internally by that customer;
  (d) OEM and White Label: embedding the Software in, or rebranding it
      as, a product, platform, framework, or library that You provide to
      third parties;
  (e) Redistribution and Resale: selling, reselling, or commercially
      redistributing the Software itself, with or without modification,
      including as a component library, UI kit, design system, theme, or
      template;
  (f) Commercial Templates: selling or commercially licensing templates,
      starters, or boilerplates built with the Software;
  (g) Builder Platforms: using the Software as a component capability of
      a low-code, no-code, UI builder, page builder, website builder,
      app builder, dashboard builder, or design-system platform offered
      to customers.

In short: build for yourself or your own organization — free. Build
software for customers — a commercial license is required.

To obtain a commercial license, see COMMERCIAL_LICENSE.md.

